WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:04.652 --> 00:00:09.805 line:88% position:50% align:center
Lesson three: site operations,
casual workers and daily reporting.

2
00:00:10.852 --> 00:00:14.045 line:88% position:50% align:center
This lesson follows the team
leader's work in the field:

3
00:00:14.055 --> 00:00:19.481 line:88% position:50% align:center
recording the people on site, and reporting
each day's activity accurately and on time.

4
00:00:21.285 --> 00:00:24.166 line:88% position:50% align:center
Team leaders sign in
using the Team Leader tab,

5
00:00:24.176 --> 00:00:27.857 line:88% position:50% align:center
with the username and
password they received by SMS.

6
00:00:28.885 --> 00:00:32.605 line:88% position:50% align:center
They arrive on My Projects:
their personal workspace.

7
00:00:33.652 --> 00:00:36.962 line:88% position:50% align:center
The four cards show the number
of projects assigned to them,

8
00:00:36.972 --> 00:00:40.921 line:88% position:50% align:center
the casual workers on their sites,
the daily logs they've submitted,

9
00:00:40.931 --> 00:00:43.375 line:88% position:50% align:center
and any unread notifications.

10
00:00:44.419 --> 00:00:47.677 line:88% position:50% align:center
Below, each assigned
project appears as a card,

11
00:00:47.687 --> 00:00:51.805 line:88% position:50% align:center
showing its SMP reference,
module package, status,

12
00:00:51.815 --> 00:00:54.454 line:88% position:50% align:center
number of casual workers and location.

13
00:00:55.519 --> 00:00:59.025 line:88% position:50% align:center
Selecting a project card
opens the project's own page,

14
00:00:59.035 --> 00:01:03.263 line:88% position:50% align:center
and the Submit Daily Log button gives
quick access to the day's report.

15
00:01:04.819 --> 00:01:08.637 line:88% position:50% align:center
As a team leader, you are the
organisation's eyes on site,

16
00:01:08.647 --> 00:01:11.560 line:88% position:50% align:center
and your responsibilities
in the system are clear.

17
00:01:12.585 --> 00:01:16.110 line:88% position:50% align:center
Keep the list of casual workers
on your projects accurate.

18
00:01:17.152 --> 00:01:20.131 line:88% position:50% align:center
Submit a daily log for each working day.

19
00:01:21.185 --> 00:01:23.818 line:88% position:50% align:center
Request additional funds
only when they are needed,

20
00:01:23.828 --> 00:01:25.348 line:88% position:50% align:center
with a clear reason.

21
00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:29.591 line:88% position:50% align:center
And mark the project
complete when, and only when,

22
00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:31.785 line:88% position:50% align:center
the work is genuinely finished.

23
00:01:33.285 --> 00:01:37.963 line:88% position:50% align:center
On the project page, a team leader sees
a progress indicator and a summary of the

24
00:01:37.973 --> 00:01:42.513 line:88% position:50% align:center
team, followed by tabs for
Overview, Casuals and Logs.

25
00:01:43.552 --> 00:01:47.006 line:88% position:50% align:center
The overview shows the
project's details: client,

26
00:01:47.016 --> 00:01:50.346 line:88% position:50% align:center
location, region, dates and team leader.

27
00:01:51.385 --> 00:01:55.177 line:88% position:50% align:center
When the work is finished, the Mark
Complete button sends the project to the

28
00:01:55.187 --> 00:01:57.059 line:88% position:50% align:center
administrator for approval.

29
00:01:57.559 --> 00:02:00.251 line:88% position:50% align:center
We'll come back to that
at the end of this lesson.

30
00:02:01.652 --> 00:02:07.013 line:88% position:50% align:center
Casual workers are added from My Casuals,
or from the Casuals tab of a project.

31
00:02:07.514 --> 00:02:09.450 line:88% position:50% align:center
Select Add Casual.

32
00:02:10.852 --> 00:02:13.310 line:88% position:50% align:center
Enter the worker's name and phone number.

33
00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.395 line:88% position:50% align:center
Both are required.

34
00:02:15.893 --> 00:02:20.681 line:88% position:50% align:center
The phone number is used to send the worker
an SMS when they're added to the project.

35
00:02:21.719 --> 00:02:26.507 line:88% position:50% align:center
Role describes the worker's job on
site, such as rigger or electrician.

36
00:02:27.008 --> 00:02:32.043 line:88% position:50% align:center
Daily Rate is optional, and records the
agreed daily rate in Kenyan shillings.

37
00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:34.982 line:88% position:50% align:center
Then choose the project.

38
00:02:35.483 --> 00:02:39.048 line:88% position:50% align:center
Team leaders can only select
the projects assigned to them.

39
00:02:40.085 --> 00:02:44.101 line:88% position:50% align:center
Select Add. The worker
is saved to the project,

40
00:02:44.111 --> 00:02:48.840 line:88% position:50% align:center
the action is recorded in the audit log,
and SMS messages go to the worker and to

41
00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:52.714 line:88% position:50% align:center
the administrator — if those
SMS events are switched on.

42
00:02:54.119 --> 00:02:57.195 line:88% position:50% align:center
The worker now appears in
the project's casual list,

43
00:02:57.205 --> 00:03:00.131 line:88% position:50% align:center
with their phone number, role and status.

44
00:03:01.185 --> 00:03:04.358 line:88% position:50% align:center
The edit button lets you
correct a worker's details.

45
00:03:04.859 --> 00:03:08.755 line:88% position:50% align:center
The delete button removes them: you'll
be asked to confirm and re-enter your

46
00:03:08.765 --> 00:03:13.722 line:88% position:50% align:center
password, and both the worker and the
administrator are informed by SMS.

47
00:03:14.785 --> 00:03:16.709 line:88% position:50% align:center
Keep this list up to date.

48
00:03:17.209 --> 00:03:20.917 line:88% position:50% align:center
The daily log uses it to
record who was present on site.

49
00:03:22.319 --> 00:03:26.710 line:88% position:50% align:center
Administrators can see every
casual worker, across all projects,

50
00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:31.495 line:88% position:50% align:center
on the All Casuals page, and
search by name, phone or role.

51
00:03:32.919 --> 00:03:36.900 line:88% position:50% align:center
Now, the most important
routine of all: the daily log.

52
00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.896 line:88% position:50% align:center
Select Submit Daily Log from My
Projects, from the Daily Logs page,

53
00:03:41.906 --> 00:03:44.116 line:88% position:50% align:center
or from the project's Logs tab.

54
00:03:45.519 --> 00:03:48.211 line:88% position:50% align:center
The Submit Daily Log form opens.

55
00:03:49.252 --> 00:03:51.618 line:88% position:50% align:center
First, select the project.

56
00:03:52.119 --> 00:03:56.523 line:88% position:50% align:center
The list shows only your assigned
projects, and when you change the project,

57
00:03:56.533 --> 00:03:59.589 line:88% position:50% align:center
the list of casual workers updates to match.

58
00:04:00.619 --> 00:04:02.777 line:88% position:50% align:center
Next, confirm the date.

59
00:04:03.277 --> 00:04:07.936 line:88% position:50% align:center
It defaults to today, but you can choose
an earlier date if you're reporting late.

60
00:04:08.985 --> 00:04:10.779 line:88% position:50% align:center
Enter the hours worked.

61
00:04:11.279 --> 00:04:16.263 line:88% position:50% align:center
The form suggests eight hours, so adjust
it to reflect the actual working day.

62
00:04:17.319 --> 00:04:21.170 line:88% position:50% align:center
In Work Done, describe clearly
what was accomplished today.

63
00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:25.632 line:88% position:50% align:center
Be specific: what was
installed, completed or tested,

64
00:04:25.642 --> 00:04:29.075 line:88% position:50% align:center
and where. This field is required.

65
00:04:30.119 --> 00:04:33.586 line:88% position:50% align:center
In Materials Used, list
the materials consumed

66
00:04:33.596 --> 00:04:37.707 line:88% position:50% align:center
— for example, mast sections,
or twenty metres of cable.

67
00:04:38.752 --> 00:04:42.668 line:88% position:50% align:center
Then tick each casual worker
who was present on site today.

68
00:04:43.719 --> 00:04:47.277 line:88% position:50% align:center
Where sites have been linked to a
project, they are recorded with the log

69
00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:50.512 line:88% position:50% align:center
automatically, so you don't
need to enter them separately.

70
00:04:51.552 --> 00:04:56.531 line:88% position:50% align:center
Select Submit. The log is saved with
your name and the time of submission,

71
00:04:56.541 --> 00:05:00.672 line:88% position:50% align:center
an entry is written to the audit log,
and the administrator receives an in-app

72
00:05:00.682 --> 00:05:05.041 line:88% position:50% align:center
notification — and an SMS,
if that event is switched on.

73
00:05:06.452 --> 00:05:11.416 line:88% position:50% align:center
Your log now appears on the Daily Logs
page, and in the project's Logs tab,

74
00:05:11.426 --> 00:05:17.464 line:88% position:50% align:center
showing the date, project, work done,
hours, workers present and materials used.

75
00:05:18.485 --> 00:05:22.342 line:88% position:50% align:center
Administrators see the same report
on their own Daily Logs page,

76
00:05:22.352 --> 00:05:26.333 line:88% position:50% align:center
which lists logs from every
team leader, most recent first.

77
00:05:27.352 --> 00:05:30.207 line:88% position:50% align:center
Submitted logs can't be
edited in the platform,

78
00:05:30.217 --> 00:05:33.325 line:88% position:50% align:center
so take a moment to check your
entries before you submit.

79
00:05:34.852 --> 00:05:37.609 line:88% position:50% align:center
Here's what happens to the
information you submit.

80
00:05:38.652 --> 00:05:42.971 line:88% position:50% align:center
Your daily log is stored centrally,
in the Firestore database.

81
00:05:44.019 --> 00:05:47.629 line:88% position:50% align:center
The administrator is alerted
through the notification centre and,

82
00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:50.135 line:88% position:50% align:center
where enabled, by SMS.

83
00:05:51.185 --> 00:05:55.251 line:88% position:50% align:center
The log appears on the Daily Logs
page and in the project's activity,

84
00:05:55.261 --> 00:05:58.330 line:88% position:50% align:center
and it counts toward the
project's progress indicator.

85
00:05:59.385 --> 00:06:03.841 line:88% position:50% align:center
Management can then review field
activity for every project in one place,

86
00:06:03.851 --> 00:06:06.934 line:88% position:50% align:center
and report it upward to the
Board and project owners.

87
00:06:07.985 --> 00:06:12.435 line:88% position:50% align:center
Remember, though: the system
records what authorised users enter.

88
00:06:12.935 --> 00:06:16.617 line:88% position:50% align:center
It doesn't independently verify
the physical work on site.

89
00:06:17.115 --> 00:06:21.141 line:88% position:50% align:center
The value of every report depends on
the accuracy and honesty of the person

90
00:06:21.151 --> 00:06:22.267 line:88% position:50% align:center
submitting it.

91
00:06:23.785 --> 00:06:28.912 line:88% position:50% align:center
When all the work on a project is finished,
open the project and select Mark Complete.

92
00:06:29.952 --> 00:06:32.917 line:88% position:50% align:center
You can add optional notes, then submit.

93
00:06:33.418 --> 00:06:38.492 line:88% position:50% align:center
The project moves to Pending Approval, and
the administrator is notified to review it.

94
00:06:39.519 --> 00:06:44.001 line:88% position:50% align:center
If the administrator sends it back, you'll
receive a notification with the reason,

95
00:06:44.011 --> 00:06:47.315 line:88% position:50% align:center
and the project returns to active
so that you can resolve it.

96
00:06:49.052 --> 00:06:52.310 line:88% position:50% align:center
To recap: keep your casual
worker list accurate,

97
00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:55.305 line:88% position:50% align:center
submit a clear daily log
for every working day,

98
00:06:55.315 --> 00:06:59.036 line:88% position:50% align:center
and mark projects complete only
when the work is truly done.

99
00:07:00.085 --> 00:07:04.112 line:88% position:50% align:center
Accurate, timely reports are what allow
management and the Board to trust the

100
00:07:04.122 --> 00:07:05.511 line:88% position:50% align:center
picture they see.

101
00:07:06.552 --> 00:07:10.253 line:88% position:50% align:center
In the next lesson, we'll look at
the financial side of the platform:

102
00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:13.801 line:88% position:50% align:center
allocations, expenditure
and additional funding.

103
00:07:16.752 --> 00:07:20.772 line:88% position:50% align:center
This training experience was
produced by KEYPOLE TECHNOLOGIES.
